WEBVTT

00:01.122 --> 00:02.204
Hi everyone.

00:02.204 --> 00:06.450
Excited to share that there's a new
feature inside of the Opportunities app.

00:06.450 --> 00:09.894
It's the Reentry tool, so follow along
for the three-minute walkthrough

00:09.894 --> 00:11.256
to see what's inside.

00:11.256 --> 00:16.163
Now when you log into Opportunities,
you will see the new Reentry page.

00:16.163 --> 00:20.049
To begin, select Get started.

00:20.049 --> 00:23.734
Next is an overview page
of the Reentry tool.

00:23.734 --> 00:29.538
Beginning with your Reentry profile,
a housing resource page

00:29.538 --> 00:36.145
that lives within the Resource Explorer,
and two topic pages with information

00:36.145 --> 00:39.589
on ID documents and housing basics.

00:39.589 --> 00:41.251
Build your Reentry profile.

00:41.251 --> 00:45.896
Select Start answering and this will
take you to an informational page.

00:45.896 --> 00:49.720
Once reviewed, you can then begin
answering a few simple questions

00:49.720 --> 00:52.323
that will take around 10 minutes
to complete.

00:52.323 --> 00:55.486
Be as honest as possible
when answering the questions.

00:55.486 --> 01:00.355
You also have the option to say
"I don't know yet" or "I'd rather not say."

01:00.355 --> 01:03.679
Once you have completed the questionnaire,

01:03.679 --> 01:07.563
it will generate a personalized
reentry checklist for you.

01:07.563 --> 01:12.108
To give it a look, select View checklist.

01:12.108 --> 01:15.192
Here you will see five time bands.

01:15.192 --> 01:18.095
The first one you can complete anytime.

01:18.095 --> 01:23.381
The next four you can complete
12 months, 6 months, 3 months,

01:23.381 --> 01:26.405
and 1 month before your release.

01:26.405 --> 01:33.710
Hit the dropdown and you can begin
checking off tasks along your way.

01:33.710 --> 01:38.457
Back on the overview page, review profile.

01:38.457 --> 01:42.343
Here you have the option to change
these answers at any time.

01:42.343 --> 01:46.709
Next, we're going to jump
into the Resource Explorer.

01:46.709 --> 01:50.575
As of now, you can browse different
types of housing resources

01:50.575 --> 01:54.341
to help you plan where you'll go
after release.

01:54.341 --> 02:04.551
You also have the ability to filter
resources down by housing, county,

02:04.551 --> 02:14.062
gender served, length of stay, weekly rent
and which groups the housing accepts.

02:14.062 --> 02:18.787
At the bottom of the Reentry tool,
you will see two topic pages:

02:18.787 --> 02:21.550
ID documents and housing basics.

02:21.550 --> 02:25.014
Inside of ID documents, you'll see
information on important

02:25.014 --> 02:28.546
identification documents,
when you're going to need them

02:28.546 --> 02:32.771
and how to apply for them
while you're still inside.

02:32.771 --> 02:37.477
Click on these tabs to learn
more about each document.

02:37.477 --> 02:40.921
At the bottom, we have some frequently
asked questions you can review.

02:40.921 --> 02:47.949
Inside of the housing basics page,
you will see housing options for reentry,

02:47.949 --> 02:51.834
six steps to plan for housing
before your release,

02:51.834 --> 02:57.060
and also a section for
frequently asked questions.

02:57.060 --> 02:59.074
And that brings us to the end.

02:59.074 --> 03:02.346
This is a tool to prepare you for reentry.

03:02.346 --> 03:07.243
And remember, when preparation meets
opportunity, success is inevitable.

03:07.243 --> 03:09.670
Thank you for your time
and have a great day.
